                <pb facs="0744" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/11967: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vichy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-06-12T19:00:00+02:00">June 12, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 12—5:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>680. Department’s 470, June 10, 10 a.m. [<hi rendition="#italic">p.m.</hi>]. I
                    delivered the oral message and <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> to
                    Marshal Pétain at 6:00 this afternoon.</p>
                <p>Report of interview follows.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
